2. Research Plan: Based on the hit genes identified, I will prioritize testing genes in four interconnected pathways: (1) T cell receptor signaling components and kinases related to identified hits (SYK is marginal, so test related kinases like FES, CSK, PAG1); (2) JAK-STAT pathway members beyond those tested (JAK3, STAT2, STAT5A/B variants, and negative regulators like PTPN2, PTPN1); (3) NF-kB pathway components and regulators (NFKB1 tested but marginal, test RELA pathway members, IKBA, NFKBIE, RELB variants); (4) Th1 differentiation factors and chromatin remodelers (SETDB1 positive, test related epigenetic regulators like EHMT1, KMT2D, JMJD3). The reasoning is that hit genes cluster in T cell activation and Th1 differentiation, so systematic testing of their pathway partners will identify additional regulators.

